      "worked_solution": "Note that the line passes through the points $(-4,-1)$ and $(4,0).$ So, we let $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(-4,-1)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(4,0),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-(-1)}{4-(-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the line is $m=\\frac{1}{8}.$",
